@startuml
title Content Studio - protected foundation

actor Administrator
participant "Frontend" as Frontend
participant "JWT + admin guard" as Auth
participant "Feature flag guard" as Flag
participant "Catalog service" as Catalog
participant "Deployment config" as Config

Administrator -> Frontend: Open /adm/estudio
Frontend -> Auth: GET /content-studio/catalog
Auth -> Flag: authenticated administrator
Flag -> Catalog: content-studio enabled
Catalog --> Frontend: versioned audiences, stages, capabilities

Administrator -> Frontend: Open provider configuration
Frontend -> Auth: GET /ai-management/providers
Auth -> Flag: authenticated administrator
Flag -> Config: provider-admin enabled
Config --> Frontend: safe metadata only\n(no secret values)

note right of Catalog
No generation, persistence or
publication occurs on GET.
end note

Administrator -> Frontend: Choose audience (Baby, children, teens, adults)
Frontend -> Auth: POST /content-studio/packages { audience, theme, ... }
Auth -> Flag: authenticated administrator
Flag -> "Create package service": content-studio enabled
"Create package service" -> "Package repository": selected audience catalog\n(omitted audience: legacy four-track package)
"Package repository" --> Frontend: persisted package and stages
Administrator -> Frontend: Select stage, edit fields, preview, save
Frontend -> Auth: PATCH stage content
note over Frontend
Old multi-audience packages retain category navigation.
Drafts stay separate per stage while switching categories.
end note

@enduml

